  "body": "[MSC2675](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/2675) says that `/sync` is one of the APIs which should bundle aggregations:\r\n\r\n> `GET /sync`, only for room sections in the response where `limited` field is `true`; this amounts to all rooms in the response if the `since` request parameter was not passed, also known as an initial sync.\r\n\r\nCurrently it always disables bundled aggregations for this endpoint, see #5220.\r\n\r\nWe should also double check the other endpoints:\r\n\r\n* [x] `GET /rooms/{roomId}/messages` -- [see code](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a265fbd397ae72b2d3ea4c9310591ff1d0f3e05c/synapse/handlers/pagination.py#L545-L558)\r\n* [x] `GET /rooms/{roomId}/context` -- [see code](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a265fbd397ae72b2d3ea4c9310591ff1d0f3e05c/synapse/rest/client/room.py#L709-L723) (note that this doesn't bundle them for state events, unclear if this is \"fine\" or not)\r\n* [x] `GET /rooms/{roomId}/event/{eventId}` -- [see code](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a265fbd397ae72b2d3ea4c9310591ff1d0f3e05c/synapse/rest/client/room.py#L664-L666)\r\n* [ ] `GET /sync`\r\n* [x] `GET /relations` -- see #11087",
